# Configuration for gigalixir-buildpack-phoenix-static, the third buildpack in .buildpacks (after the Elixir
# buildpack, before Distillery). On each Gigalixir deploy it builds the frontend assets as follows:
#
#   1. Picks the Node version. With no `node_version` set here, it uses the `nodejs` entry in .tool-versions,
#      so local dev, CircleCI (.circleci/config.yml) and Gigalixir all share one pin. An explicit
#      `node_version` in this file would take precedence over .tool-versions.
#   2. Downloads Node, then, because yarn.lock exists, a Yarn Classic (1.x) release matching `yarn_version`
#      below. The buildpack only supports Yarn Classic, npm and pnpm, so the project cannot move to Yarn 2+
#      until the buildpack does. Keep `yarn_version` in sync with `packageManager` in package.json.
#   3. Runs `yarn install --check-files --pure-lockfile`, which also triggers the `postinstall` script.
#   4. Runs the `compile` script in the repo root: `npm run compile-production` (webpack, which needs
#      NODE_OPTIONS=--openssl-legacy-provider because webpack 4 uses md4 hashing) and then
#      `mix phx.digest --no-vsn`.
#
# Production deploys force a clean build (the GIGALIXIR-CLEAN header in the `deploy` job of
# .circleci/config.yml), so Node and Yarn are fetched fresh each time. Staging deploys reuse the build cache.
yarn_version=1.22.22
